{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>If its owner is with it.</b> At its work, at the time of the loan." "<b>He shall not make restitution.</b> For an ordinary borrower, on the understanding implied here, is giving a gift on the understanding that it will be returned; and since he made no stipulation, he is not obligated to return it except while it is still intact. For even according to the one who says that a gift on condition to return obligates in cases of accident — that is because the condition of 'on condition that' invalidates the gift if the condition is not fulfilled. But here, since it is a gift on the understanding to return, without a condition that would invalidate the gift if he does not return it, so long as it is in the recipient's hands it is his, even if he does not return it afterward, and he will not be liable for anything that happens to it, even through negligence. Accordingly the tradition came that every bailee is exempt when the owner is with him, even through negligence."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:48.064668534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}